\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Evaluating a Laurent symbol on a magnetic pair}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Let #{X,Y} be unitaries on a finite complex Hermitian space #{V} satisfying #{YX=\ue^{\ui\phi}XY}. Let #{W} be another finite complex Hermitian space. Write #{E_y} for the eigenspace of #{Y} of eigenvalue #{\ue^{\ui y}}. For a function #{f} on the angle circle with values in #{\operatorname{End}(W)}, let #{f(Y)} act by #{f(y)} on the first factor of #{W\otimes E_y}. The \newvocab{ordered evaluation} of the Laurent symbol
##{F(x,y)=\sum_{s=-1}^{1} f_s(y)\ue^{\ui sx}}
is #{B=\sum_s f_s(Y)X^s} on #{W\otimes V}, with #{X} acting on the second factor.}

\p{For real scalar #{d(y)} write
##{H=\begin{pmatrix}d(Y)&B\\ B^\dagger&-d(Y)\end{pmatrix}.}
The \newvocab{frozen symbol} is the same block at scalar #{x,y}, with #{F(x,y)} in place of #{B} and its adjoint below. This order of substituting the shifts agrees with the upper entry in \ref{fdip-01A6}.}
